{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Hecke.WedderburnWeightDegeneracyReal","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Hecke.WedderburnWeightDegeneracyReal","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Hecke.WedderburnWeightDegeneracy"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.WedderburnWeightDegeneracy.zC_ne_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.WedderburnWeightDegeneracy.zC_ne_one","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/WedderburnWeightDegeneracyReal.lean#L53-L58","doc":"Immediate corollary: `z_C = 1` has no positive solution. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.WedderburnWeightDegeneracy.zC_le_half","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.WedderburnWeightDegeneracy.zC_le_half","kind":"theorem","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/WedderburnWeightDegeneracyReal.lean#L42-L51","doc":"**The convention-C loop value never reaches 1**, for any `u > 0`: `z_C ≤ 1/2`.\n\nThe corpus (`qbeta-counit-closed-form.md`) says the trivial loop value \"is never\nattained on the substrate\", which is a statement about `q_0`.  This is the\nstronger fact: under convention C the Frobenius counit `ε = tr_M|_{z=1}` is\nunreachable as a Markov trace at EVERY `q`, not merely at the anchor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.WedderburnWeightDegeneracy.y21_at_zD_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.WedderburnWeightDegeneracy.y21_at_zD_pos","kind":"theorem","line":26,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/WedderburnWeightDegeneracyReal.lean#L26-L40","doc":"**THE RESULT.  The `(2,1)` Wedderburn weight is strictly positive at the\ncanonical loop value, for every nonzero real `q`.**\n\n`y_(2,1)(z_D) = q²/(q²+1)²` is a manifestly positive rational function, so the\nblock never degenerates: there is no convention-D analogue of the convention-C\nhadronic melt at any real `q`.  A scope-(b) exclusion of the Wedderburn /\nGram-degeneracy route with the invariant exhibited — it says nothing about a\ntransition produced by some other mechanism. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.WedderburnWeightDegeneracy.zD_ne_neg_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.WedderburnWeightDegeneracy.zD_ne_neg_inv","kind":"theorem","line":15,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/WedderburnWeightDegeneracyReal.lean#L15-L24","doc":"**`z_D = −1/q` has no real solution at all**, since it forces\n`q⁴ + q² + 1 = 0`.  Convention D never reaches the second root either. ","signatureChunk":0}]}